issue_context:
Change `PublicApi::from_rustdoc_json(path, Options::default())` to `public_api::Builder::from_rustdoc_json(path).build()`
Instead of this public API for the `public-api` lib:

```rust
    // Derive the public API from the rustdoc JSON
    let mut options = public_api::Options::default();
    options.omit_blanket_impls = true;
    options.omit_auto_trait_impls = true;
    let public_api = public_api::PublicApi::from_rustdoc_json(path, options).unwrap();
```

I want the public API to be this:

```rust
    // Derive the public API from the rustdoc JSON
    let public_api = public_api::Builder::from_rustdoc_json(path)
        .omit_blanket_impls(true)
        .omit_auto_trait_impls(true)
        .build()
        .unwrap();
```

which has the following benefits:
* nicer and simpler API
* symmetry with the `rustdoc_json::Builder` API

I have made a prototype commit that passed CI: https://github.com/Enselic/cargo-public-api/pull/293

Doing it properly with a proper public API deprecation path is more work, however. And this is not top prio for me right now. So I am creating this issue to make my long-term intention visible to others.

